import Mathlib
/-!
# Table B5 data (R14 / r14a): the exact rational constants of the B5
# Procrustes rigidity package

This module is deliberately self-contained: it imports only `Mathlib`,
imports no in-repo solution module, and is imported only by
`ThomsonN9/TableB5.lean`.  It materialises, as explicit `ℚ` literals,
the constant layer of the L4 Procrustes theorem
(`numerics/bounds/results/l4.json`, read-only, re-derived here through
the independent second implementation of `numerics/bounds/r14_b5_data.py`:
stdlib-Fraction Newton square-root envelopes and a symbolic engine over
ℚ[ρ,√3]/(ρ² = 1−z², (√3)² = 3); provenance = sha256 of l4.json and
local_min.json, recorded in `results/r14_b5_data.json` — the constants are
exact Fractions, so there is no dyadic rounding surface here):

* `zLo`, `zHi` — the TTP z-box, identical to the strict isolation
  interval `zStarIntervalMpmath` of `results/local_min.json`;
* `l3`, `u1` — the recorded interval-Sylvester eigenvalue bounds
  λ₃ ≥ l₃, λ₁ ≤ u₁, dominated by the diagonal route
  (6·zLo² ≥ l₃, 9/2 − 3·zLo² ≤ u₁, zHi² < 1/2);
* `s1Up`, `s3Dn`, `sqrt72Up` — the 200-bit rational square-root
  envelopes σ₁ ≤ s1Up, σ₃ ≥ s3Dn, √72 ≤ sqrt72Up;
* `CInner`, `CVal`, `CChord`, `deltaMax` — the four assembled
  constants, with the four assembly identities as `norm_num` theorems
  (636-bit Fractions, D56 probe ②);
* the twelve `S**` endpoints — the recorded l4.json `S_interval`
  entries (S22 endpoints are exactly 6·zLo² / 6·zHi²; S00/S11 are
  strictly widened ρ-enclosures; the off-diagonal recorded intervals
  are symmetric and contain 0);
* `diagQ` — the ℚ diagonal quadratic form of the TTP family,
  (3(1−z²)+3/2)(v₀²+v₁²) + 6z²v₂², with three fixed random rational
  spot checks (seed 20261016, z on the 2⁻⁴⁰ grid inside the z-box,
  v on the /64 grid) whose expected values are independently computed
  in Python `Fraction` and cross-checked by the gate's symbolic
  row-expansion second implementation.

Honest scope note (B5-first-piece boundary): the analytic body
d_P(X,Y) ≤ C·δ (l4_procrustes.py proof steps 1–6: projection split /
polar decomposition / rotation normalisation) is NOT part of this file;
`TableB5.lean` proves the constant-layer validity theorems only.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

namespace ThomsonN9.TableB5Data

